+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value |
+| ------ | ----- |
+| Issue  | 37    |
+| Status | Draft |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` checks the input of a tool call against the tool's declared `inputSchema` before the executor runs. A call the schema rejects never reaches the executor. The rejection is returned to the model as a tool result, so the model can correct the call within the tool-round budget instead of ending the turn.
+
+## Rejection
+
+- A call whose input omits a required property is answered with a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names that property and the `required` constraint, and the executor is not invoked ([validated by: answers a call missing a required property with a rejection naming it, without running the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L28)).
+- A call whose input gives a property the wrong type is answered with a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the property path and the expected type, and never contains the offending value ([validated by: names the property path and expected type for a wrong-typed value, and never echoes the value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L43)).
+- The orchestrator hands a rejection to the model as a tool result, so a corrected retry within the tool-round budget completes the turn and `processMessage` resolves ([validated by: hands a rejected tool call back to the model so a corrected retry completes the turn](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L65)).
+
+## Registration
+
+- Registering a tool whose `inputSchema` cannot be compiled throws at `register`, not mid-conversation, and the error names the tool ([validated by: fails registration of a tool whose inputSchema cannot be compiled, and the error names the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L54)).
